HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_70f52f79, "an `extern constant`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5ecf85f5, "a `str` is built by this runtime, so no C header holds one: declare it `cstr` and read it with `validated`, which copies and may fail (\302\2474.20)");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_612fabdb, "a `constant` names a value, and `()` is a type rather than a value");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_76e6282d, "a function value Heroes calls must be one this compiler emitted, and this asks the header for one of C's. Declare it `ptr` if the program only hands it back to C");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_760ac0ad, "a `str` is this runtime's own value, with a reference count before its bytes, so no C struct holds one: declare the field `cstr` and read it with `validated`, which copies and may fail");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_380698fc, "a C struct holds a pointer to its elements, never the elements: declare the field `ptr` and reach them through the header's own accessors");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7357b0c8, "`T?` is this language's own two-word value and no header declares one: a C function reports failure in its result or an out-parameter (\302\2474.19)");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_32c7b346, "`()` is a type rather than a value, so nothing can hold one \342\200\224 drop the field");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_59aa1d79, "a record can hold another only if the header declares that one too: move it into this `extern` group, or declare the field `ptr` if C holds a pointer to it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4c535382, "this group has no spelling for that: a field is a number, `bool`, `ptr`, `cstr`, another record of the group, or a fixed array of one");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3855f106, "`()` names no value, so there is no argument to pass: as a *result* it is C's `void`, which a parameter list has no spelling for. Drop the parameter, or declare the type the header uses");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_26f94c26, "an `@` parameter is C's out-parameter, so this asks C to WRITE a function value here, and a function value Heroes calls must be one this compiler emitted. Declare it `@");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7c22a36c, ": ptr` if the program only stores what C writes, and pass it back to C to be called");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1dc6f5a3, "ffi_constant_type");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7f4d9cbe, "ffi_parameter_type");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4aced738, "nothing names this function as a freer");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_605aa6ed, "the mark is on the type it is for");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_14b5465c, "owned_needs_cstr");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_339868ca, "`owned` marks a `cstr`, and ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_26a3abd2, " is a `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3732bbc, "`owned <freer>` says C writes a string THROUGH this cell and the compiler frees it with that function, so it belongs on a `@x: cstr` out-parameter or on a `cstr` result. On anything else it says nothing the compiler can act on");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6d12dccf, "the mark is on a cell");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4dd1fb4e, "`owned` marks a cell C writes THROUGH, and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_429b9256, "` is passed by value");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_246be35d, "`owned <freer>` belongs on a `@x: cstr` out-parameter or on a `cstr` result, because it says the compiler frees what C wrote there. A parameter the caller hands IN is the opposite direction: mark it `consumes` if the call ends that value's life");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4eb44276, "no extern declares it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7df95e0, "unknown_freer");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_708d9dc, "` frees nothing here: no `extern` in this module declares it, so `owned ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_69bca327, "` names a function the compiler cannot call");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_684a6265, "` is a Heroes function in this program; a freer is the C function that owns the allocation, declared in a group");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_71a9f026, "declare `function ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6ba05600, "(p: ptr)` in a group of this module \342\200\224 the header that group names is what clang checks the freer against");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_638e4f74, "\302\2474.19: the compiler frees an `owned` string by calling the freer by name, so the name has to be one this module's headers know");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_75651389, "freer_arity");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_b55ab14, "` takes ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6021ae94, " parameters, and a freer for an `owned` string is handed exactly one: the string");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_15437021, "name the function that frees THIS string \342\200\224 `free` for `strdup`, `sqlite3_free` for SQLite's own \342\200\224 or drop the `owned ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_54d1314d, "` mark and free it yourself");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_dc6a322, "fine");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2687966e, "a one-parameter extern of this module");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_37b4f297, "owned_freer_called");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3c789acd, "` is what frees an `owned` string in this program, so the compiler already calls it \342\200\224 calling it here frees the string twice");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_17338d7, "the `owned ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7ae3c839, "` that says so is ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_62a1a65, "\302\2474.19: a marked string is handed over as a `str?`, already copied \342\200\224 the bytes C gave you are gone by the time you hold it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3f3ff731, "delete this call and let the compiler free it, or delete the `owned ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_282a7421, "release");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2dfda7a5, "expected `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7a5d94f6, "`, found `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_25d7e1cf, "` takes two of one type \342\200\224 two integers of the SAME width, or two floats of the same width \342\200\224 and found `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_733e5991, "one side is text, so no `to_<width>` can help \342\200\224 those answer a number, and `+` on a `str` wants a `str`. Render the other side: `\"n is \" + n.to_str()`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_533204fc, "convert one side: `to_f64(x)` cannot fail, and `to_i64(x)` or another `to_<width>(x)` gives a `T?` because the number may not fit");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_50c417a8, "bad_operand");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4858290b, ", found `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6190a1bb, "a `cstr` is C's string, not this language's \342\200\224 `c.validated()` copies one into a `str?`, which is `null_cstr` for a null pointer and `not_text` for bytes that are not UTF-8");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_66070846, "unordered_element");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_19f11d9f, "`sort` orders arrays of numbers, `str` and `bool` \342\200\224 `[");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_18204300, "]` is none of those");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3274b0a6, "` is a type parameter, so this line cannot know whether it has an order \342\200\224 take the comparison as a parameter instead, `less: (function(candidate: ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_61b5d126, ", best: ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1c690931, ") -> bool)`, and name its arguments at the call, `less(candidate: x, best: best)`: two parameters of one type are named in the type, so the order of the two is checked for you");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_65446aba, ", which has no order the language can produce. Sort a key you can name instead \342\200\224 build `[i64]`, `[str]` or `[bool]` from the values and order that");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5f6ff10d, "the ordered types are `i8` `i16` `i32` `i64`, `u8` `u16` `u32` `u64`, `f32` `f64`, `str` and `bool`. Sort a key you can name instead \342\200\224 build an array of one of those from the values and order that");
