HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_44fb569, "every payload is ordered");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_11831e5f, "` is `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_751826e1, "`, a record");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2face523, "every field is ordered");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_24abd5d8, "`str`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1f3e1603, "`@x` where `x: cstr @ s.lease()`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_70336d0, "a run of bytes \342\200\224 `i8[N]`, `u8[N]` or `[u8]`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_38c679f7, "a fixed run of bytes \342\200\224 `i8[N]` or `u8[N]`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_58563470, "not a lend, a lease or a release");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2e580070, "`counted_by` says how far C reads or writes through a `ptr`, and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_bb57eea, "` is not one");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1050bc05, "` names no other parameter of `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_779bc888, "` \342\200\224 the extent is a sibling in the same signature, the one C reads the count from");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6b6d68b3, "` is not an integer C takes by value, so it cannot say how far C reads \342\200\224 an extent is `i32`, `u64`, or another width the header spells");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5fe7554a, "no such sibling");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6ef2bb26, "` is an `@` out-parameter, and no lend can stand in an `@` position");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_32734459, "` is not a `cstr` or a `ptr`, and only those two are ever lent");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_675a15f, "` is a `ptr` that declares no extent, and a `ptr` lend reaches only a parameter declared `counted_by` \342\200\224 nothing is ever lent here, so the word is dead text; write `counted_by <n> lent`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_47f09254, "this declaration is already on the route");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_42d22643, "no handle here");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1a32ddb1, "no payload reaches a handle");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_65a39e5c, "every field is the program's own");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_16a0dff, "a function of this program");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_636e998e, "not a function");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1d3010f6, "not a declared function");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1c7b1c96, "not an argument of this call");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7e152b8d, "not an extern call");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7da10fc3, "not an argument");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4e3da0d2, "past the signature, which arity refuses");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_625b7abc, "uncounted");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_23befc98, "`.cstr()`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4d6e0c11, "`.ptr()`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5216f75b, "cstr_escapes");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2b9d4a87, "`.cstr()` lends this string to C for the length of one call (\302\2474.19), and a lend may stand only as an argument of a call \342\200\224 here it stands somewhere the pointer outlives the bytes it points into");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1ee20535, "pass it directly as an argument of the call that reads it. The bytes belong to the `str`, and the slot holding one is released when its function returns OR when the same expression runs again, whichever comes first \342\200\224 so a lend kept past its call is reading freed memory by the next iteration. A wrapper that reaches C from another module takes a `str` and lends inside itself");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7b9ab2f, "building a `record` of an `extern` group is not such a call: the pointer becomes a field of a value the statement hands on, and it outlives the bytes. Copy the bytes with `x: cstr @ s.lease()` and hold the cell, or hold the `str` and lend at each call");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_730ccfaa, "cstr_out_of_heroes");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_7ab4d146, "` answers `cstr`, and a `cstr` is C's pointer rather than this language's string (\302\2474.19) \342\200\224 only a function inside an `extern` group may answer one");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3836c972, "answer `str` and let the caller lend it with `.cstr()` at the call that reads it. A `cstr` handed out of a Heroes function points into bytes this function stops owning when it returns");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5a834eb3, "cstr_in_a_record");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_28a2e793, "` holds a `cstr`, and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_34a1df30, "` is not a record of an `extern` group \342\200\224 a C pointer parked in a Heroes record outlives the bytes it points into (\302\2474.19)");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_28d8764f, "hold a `str` in the field and lend it with `.cstr()` at the call that reads it. A group's `record` may hold a `cstr`, because there the fields are the header's and C owns the bytes");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_8365ae6, "lend_needs_a_header");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_d1d63e3, "`.cstr()` lends a `str` to C for one call, and it may stand only as an argument of a function declared in an `extern` group \342\200\224 here the callee is this program's own, and no declaration of this program can say what becomes of the pointer");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_42f7192f, "lend at the call that reaches C: a wrapper takes the `str` and lends inside itself \342\200\224 `function say(text: str) -> i32` returning `puts(s: text.cstr())` \342\200\224 which is the shape \302\2474.19 prescribes as the route out of a module, and the header is asked where the lend is made");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2abd0258, "lend_kept");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6e466c16, " lends bytes to C for this call and no longer, and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4810a221, "` is not declared to let them go \342\200\224 a C parameter without `lent` is assumed to keep what it is handed, and bytes kept past the call are read after the program has changed or freed them");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_574f798a, ": cstr lent`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_42ba0fb3, ": ptr counted_by ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_65f8029a, " lent`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1f001b4a, "if the header's function only reads or fills through the pointer while it runs, say so where it is declared: ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4e06a1e3, " \342\200\224 a claim about C that nothing here can check, which is why it is not written for you. If C FREES what it is handed, no mark and no lease makes the call sound, and nothing in the language yet declares that parameter");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3fb0ff53, "if C does keep the address, a field has no lease: hand C memory it owns \342\200\224 allocate through the header's own allocator, copy the bytes in, and let C dispose of it \342\200\224 because the field dies with its record and nothing extends that. And if C frees what it is handed, neither route works");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_11ea31b9, "if C does keep the pointer, hand it bytes that outlive the call: `x: cstr @ s.lease()`, and `end_lease(@x)` once C is done with them. And if C frees what it is handed, neither route works: a lease is freed by `end_lease` and nothing else");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_2be9f475, "field_lend_escapes");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_cbd604f, "`.ptr()` lends this field's address to C for the length of one call (\302\2474.19), and a lend may stand only as an argument of a call \342\200\224 here it stands somewhere the pointer outlives the record it points into");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_72281fe7, "pass it directly as an argument of the call that reads or fills it. The bytes belong to the record, which is a value: the slot holding it is released when its function returns, so an address kept past its call points into memory the next statement may reuse. A C function that keeps the pointer needs the bytes copied, which is what `validated_bytes` does for text");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_148864e, "field_lend_needs_a_place");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5718eb8b, "`.ptr()` lends a field's address to C, so the field must be one this program can still name \342\200\224 here the bytes belong to a value nothing holds");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_21b57ab1, "bind the record first and lend the field of the binding: `s = make()` and then `s.name.ptr()`. C may write through this pointer, and a write into a value nothing holds lands in storage the next statement reuses. To READ a field's text without holding the record, `validated_bytes` copies the bytes out and needs no place");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_511aa506, "field_lend_needs_a_header");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_79a76a2b, "`.ptr()` lends a field's address to C, and it may stand only as an argument of a function declared in an `extern` group \342\200\224 here the callee is this program's own, and no header says whether it writes through the pointer or how far it reads");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4aa633de, "lend at the call that reaches C. A wrapper takes the record by value, or as `@`, and lends the field inside itself \342\200\224 `function total(s: Slot) -> i64` returning `slot_sum(p: s.nsap.ptr(), n: 8)` \342\200\224 which is the shape \302\2474.19 prescribes as the route out of a module, and the header is asked where the lend is made");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_42ee5a16, "field_lend_uncounted");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_f4b8e2a, "`.ptr()` lends a field's address to C with an extent this call states, and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_20789944, "` does not say which argument the extent is \342\200\224 so nothing can check the number against the field");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_57632de9, "declare the relation the header already has: `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3db269a1, ": ptr counted_by <the parameter that carries the count>` in the `extern` group, followed by `lent` where the call keeps nothing of the address \342\200\224 a parameter without that word is assumed to keep it, and the lend is refused there next. The compiler then compares the number against the field's own size, in C, wherever the call states a constant \342\200\224 an overstated one reads and WRITES past the field, silently, at exit 0");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_19e58179, "field_lend_extent");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4fc9aa8f, "` lends a field of ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1d43e91c, " bytes, and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_156b6e20, "` states ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_29e2bd20, "` is declared `counted_by ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_67516ed2, "`, and C read the field's own size from the header");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_54ffd9e9, "C reads and writes exactly the bytes this number says, so a larger one reaches past the field into whatever the header put beside it \342\200\224 a sibling of the same record, silently, at exit 0. Write the field's own length, or lend a longer field");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_32cffa27, "state the field's own length, ");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_50d45832, "field_lend_written");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_543247de, "` lends a field of `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_12fb67e4, "` to `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_33c6a1f8, "`, and the header declares that parameter `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_8edaac9, "` \342\200\224 C may write through it, and `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1d41ce71, "` is not a `@` name");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_1b762846, "\302\2474.4: only a declared `@` name can be mutated, and a C write is a mutation. Declare `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_724f788d, "` with `@` \342\200\224 a `@` cell, or a `@` parameter \342\200\224 and the bytes C writes land where this program reads them back. To only READ the field, lend it to a parameter the header declares `const`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_4a09d1b8, "lease_escapes");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5e8ac22d, "` is a lease \342\200\224 a copy of the bytes that C may read until `end_lease(@");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_fa9ada4, ")` \342\200\224 and its name may stand only as an argument of a call; here it is copied, and the copy would outlive the release");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_401a2956, "pass `");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_20c5db15, "` directly to the call that reads it. The release nulls this one cell, so a pointer that lives anywhere else keeps pointing at freed bytes");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_19f49906, "building a `record` of an `extern` group is not such a call: the field keeps the pointer past `end_lease(@");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_525c8a0f, ")`, and C then reads freed bytes. Pass the cell to each call that reads it instead of storing it");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_6ef43575, "lease_written");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_d1bbcb8, "` is a lease, and the only write a lease cell takes after its declaration is `end_lease(@");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_a9f17e9, ")` \342\200\224 a value stored over it would leak the bytes it held, or free bytes nobody leased");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_5d4cdc84, "declare a second cell for the second lease. One cell, one `.lease()`, one `end_lease`");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_40ffd478, "end_lease_of_no_lease");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_15703dd3, "`end_lease` frees what `.lease()` made, and it takes the cell that holds it: `end_lease(@x)` where `x: cstr @ s.lease()` \342\200\224 this argument is not such a cell");
HERO_STR_STATIC(hero_str_3a3f4171, "a lend (`.cstr()`), a pointer from C and a literal are freed by whoever owns them, and this program does not; a lease copied into another cell cannot be released from there, because the release must null the one cell the pointer lives in");
